  "overview": "**Ionic Framework** is a dark-first design system anchored on `#000` canvas surfaces with `#f7f7f8` primary ink (19.6:1 contrast) and `#4d8dff` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Roboto` (26px display down to 16px body), unified by `0px` razor-sharp architectural corners and hairline `1px` structural borders.\n\nMaintained by **Ionic**. Source: published token package (https://ionicframework.com/), package `@ionic/core`. Inventory: **91** colors, **14** typography steps, and **17** documented components (MIT license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 17 component tokens with documented paddings: `8px 12px`, `6px 12px`, `10px 14px`, `6px 10px`, `8px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#000` cards; separate sibling sections using `#222222` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#000` -> `#000`) and `1px solid #222222` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#4d8dff` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#000` (dark) with `#f7f7f8` primary text and `#f7f7f8` secondary labels.\n- Use `#4d8dff` with `#f7f7f8` text (3.0:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Roboto` headings with `Roboto` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Enforce `0px` border-radius consistently across cards, inputs, and primary buttons.\n- Separate containers via `#000` surface shifts and `#222222` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of dark polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not apply rounded corners (> 0px) to structural containers or CTA buttons.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
